name: wordforge
title: Wordforge - Word Processor
version: '0.6.1-preview'
summary: Word processor for fast, private writing - DOCX, PDF and spell check
description: |
  Wordforge is a fast, native word processor and document editor for Linux. It
  runs fully offline: no account, no cloud, no browser engine inside.

  Write with real page layout, paragraph styles (Normal, Title, Headings),
  bullets and numbering, tables, pictures, bookmarks, find and replace, and
  spell check as you type. Copy and paste keeps formatting from web pages,
  Microsoft Word and LibreOffice. Print, export PDF, and open or save DOCX files
  (complex Word features are not preserved yet). Text shaping covers Hindi and
  other Indic scripts, Arabic, Hebrew, Chinese, Japanese, Korean and emoji.
  Unsaved work is recovered after a crash. Light and dark themes, a Ctrl+K
  command palette and a distraction-free focus mode keep the page in front.

  This is a developer preview: headers and footers, comments and track changes
  are still to come. Built with C++20, Qt 6 and Skia; open source under
  Apache-2.0. Also available for Windows.
base: core24
grade: stable
confinement: strict
license: Apache-2.0
links:
  website:
    - https://github.com/akmcypher/wordforge
  source-code:
    - https://github.com/akmcypher/wordforge
  issues:
    - https://github.com/akmcypher/wordforge/issues
  contact:
    - https://github.com/akmcypher/wordforge/issues
architectures: [@ARCH@]
apps:
  wordforge:
    command: bin/wordforge-launch
    plugs: [desktop, desktop-legacy, x11, wayland, home, removable-media, opengl, cups]
